Puts a relayed copy of a version this machine already wants through
quarantine matching and the brake again, as receive() did before 6730e55
(§7.5, §8.1, §8.2): the early skip of an item whose version equals, or is
dominated by, the want at its path is removed, so the copy counts toward the
relay batch's brake and is quarantined under it if that batch is held while
its own fetch goes on. No seed fails with this patch (0 to 9,999, and 0 to
499 at 2,000 steps): the relayed copy is quarantined under the relay's batch
while I5 checks the want's own, so no invariant sees it. The patch names the
rule's unit test.

